Read CLAUDE.md.

Scaffold Sprint 0.1 of Ratify: tenant isolation, auth, migrations, and the
RLS isolation gate test. Deliver exactly these files:

- go.mod (module `ratify`)
- cmd/api/main.go — HTTP server with /healthz, /api/whoami, /api/accounts
  (GET list, POST create). Builds the pool via `db.NewPool` and refuses to
  boot if `db.AssertNotPrivileged` fails.
- internal/platform/config.go — env config
- internal/platform/auth.go — OIDC verifier via go-oidc. Dev mode when
  OIDC_ISSUER is empty AND ENV != production; dev mode trusts X-Tenant-Id
  and X-User-Id headers. Production without OIDC_ISSUER is a boot error.
  Missing/invalid tenant claim → 403, not "see all".
- internal/platform/httpx.go — JSON helpers, RequestLogger (never logs
  request bodies or emails)
- internal/tenant/context.go — With/From
- internal/db/pool.go — `NewPool` (the only place pgxpool is constructed)
  and `AssertNotPrivileged`: rejects superuser, `app_migrator`, any role
  with BYPASSRLS, and any role that owns a table in the public schema.
- internal/db/tx.go — TenantTx.WithTenant, the ONLY path to the DB.
  Uses set_tenant($1) which wraps set_config(..., true). Missing context
  returns ErrNoTenant.
- internal/account/repository.go — List has NO tenant predicate (RLS
  supplies it). Create uses current_tenant() for tenant_id, never client
  input.
- internal/account/handler.go
- migrations/000001_init.up.sql — set_tenant(), current_tenant() (uses
  current_setting('app.tenant_id', true), returns NULL when unset),
  tenants table, accounts table with UNIQUE (tenant_id, id), ENABLE + FORCE
  RLS on both, accounts_isolation policy (USING + WITH CHECK), indexes on
  (tenant_id, created_at) and (tenant_id, lower(domain)). Tables are owned
  by app_migrator, never by app_user.
- migrations/000001_init.down.sql
- deploy/initdb/01-roles.sql — app_user, app_migrator, ferriskey_user
  roles; ferriskey database; schema grants. Dev passwords only. No role
  gets BYPASSRLS. app_user: SELECT on tenants; SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE
  on accounts; no DDL.
- deploy/Dockerfile.api — multi-stage, distroless
- deploy/.env.example
- deploy/docker-compose.yml — postgres, redis, migrate, api. Every service
  has mem_limit and cpus matching the CLAUDE.md budget table. FerrisKey is
  profile-gated `oidc`. All images pinned to a specific tag.
- tests/tenant_isolation_test.go — runs as app_user. Four subtests: sees
  only own rows, no tenant context fails closed, raw query outside wrapper
  sees nothing, cannot insert into another tenant.
- Makefile — init, up, down, migrate, test, psql, seed, clean, budget
  (`make budget` sums compose mem_limit and fails above 14 GB)
- README.md — run instructions, the OIDC enable steps, the note that
  set_tenant MUST use transaction scope (and why SET SESSION is forbidden).

Agent acceptance:
